{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/api/books?bibkeys=OLID:OL27219418M,OLID:OL27701385M,OLID:OL27912422M,OLID:OL29763202M,OLID:OL32683083M,OLID:OL36334773M,OLID:OL48166565M&jscmd=details&format=json","file":"data/metadata1000_261025/raw/library-afaf5bfa047f2598.json","retrieved":"2026-10-25T14:38:54.177Z","status":200,"data":{"OLID:OL27219418M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL27219418M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27219418M/Pax_Romana","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27219418M/Pax_Romana","details":{"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Introduction. A glory greater than war / The Pax Romana","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Part one. Republic. The rise of Rome","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"War","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Friends and rivals","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Traders and settlers","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"'How much did you make?'- Government","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Provincials and Kings","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Part two. Principate. Emperors","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Rebellion","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Resistance, rioting and robbery","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Imperial governors","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Life under Roman rule","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"The army and the frontiers","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Garrisons and raids","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Beyond the Pax Romana","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Conclusion. Peace and war.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Best-selling author Adrian Goldsworthy turns his attention to the Pax Romana, the famous peace and prosperity brought by the Roman Empire at its height in the first and second centuries AD. Yet the Romans were conquerors, imperialists who took by force a vast empire stretching from the Euphrates to the Atlantic coast. Ruthless, Romans won peace not through coexistence but through dominance; millions died and were enslaved during the creation of their empire. Pax Romana examines how the Romans came to control so much of the world and asks whether traditionally favorable images of the Roman peace are true. Goldsworthy vividly recounts the rebellions of the conquered, examining why they broke out, why most failed, and how they became exceedingly rare. He reveals that hostility was just one reaction to the arrival of Rome and that from the outset, conquered peoples collaborated, formed alliances, and joined invaders, causing resistance movements to fade away."},"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223114699680","urn:sfpl:31223114699706","urn:sfpl:31223114699698","urn:bwbsku:O8-CDO-799","urn:bwbsku:P7-BFD-135"],"subject_times":["Empire, 30 B.C.-284 A.D."],"full_title":"Pax Romana war, peace, and conquest in the Roman world","lc_classifications":["DG276.5 .G65 2016","DG276.G65 2016"],"key":"/books/OL27219418M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL528991A","name":"Adrian Keith Goldsworthy"}],"subtitle":"war, peace, and conquest in the Roman world","subjects":["History"],"isbn_13":["9780300178821"],"pagination":"ix, 513 pages, 16 unnumbered pages of plates","source_records":["marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run05.mrc:369726973:3858","bwb:9780300178821","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-08-13","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-06-08","idb:9780300178821"],"title":"Pax Romana","lccn":["2016941493"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},"number_of_pages":513,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"dewey_decimal_class":["937.06"],"subject_places":["Rome"],"isbn_10":["0300178824"],"publish_date":"2016","publish_country":"ctu","by_statement":"Adrian Goldsworthy","oclc_numbers":["941874968"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL20039383W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"publishers":["Yale University Press"],"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-07-19T17:21:51.199832"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-12-19T21:42:23.698915"}}},"OLID:OL27701385M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL27701385M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27701385M/Pax_Romana","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27701385M/Pax_Romana","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9137611-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Yale University Press"],"subtitle":"War, Peace and Conquest in the Roman World","covers":[9137611],"physical_format":"hardcover","full_title":"Pax Romana War, Peace and Conquest in the Roman World","lc_classifications":["","DG271 .G65 2016"],"key":"/books/OL27701385M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2749695A","name":"Adrian Goldsworthy"}],"source_records":["amazon:0297864289","bwb:9780297864288","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-025.mrc:46939346:1515","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_067.bib.mrc:108728403:4174"],"title":"Pax Romana","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Source title: Pax Romana: War, Peace and Conquest in the Roman World"},"identifiers":{"amazon":["0297864289"]},"isbn_13":["9780297864288"],"isbn_10":["0297864289"],"publish_date":"2016","works":[{"key":"/works/OL20472896W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:KP-825-821"],"oclc_numbers":["956956960","920712782"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The Pax Romana is famous for having provided a remarkable period of peace and stability, rarely seen before or since. Yet the Romans were first and foremost conquerors, imperialists who took by force a vast empire stretching from the Euphrates in the east to the Atlantic coast in the west. Their peace meant Roman victory and was brought about by strength and dominance rather than co-existence with neighbours. The Romans were aggressive and ruthless, and during the creation of their empire millions died or were enslaved."},"number_of_pages":513,"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-11-16T03:47:42.717355"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-05-17T02:49:17.831031"}}},"OLID:OL27912422M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL27912422M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27912422M/Pax_Romana","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27912422M/Pax_Romana","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9269982-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Weidenfeld & Nicholson"],"classifications":{},"source_records":["bwb:9781474604376","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-06-14"],"title":"Pax Romana","identifiers":{},"isbn_13":["9781474604376"],"covers":[9269982,9269981],"physical_format":"Paperback","publish_date":"2017","key":"/books/OL27912422M","works":[{"key":"/works/OL20472896W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lc_classifications":["DG276.5"],"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:KQ-078-084","urn:bwbsku:P7-BAG-183"],"latest_revision":8,"revision":8,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-02-13T14:01:26.797246"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-01-14T18:34:48.156858"}}},"OLID:OL29763202M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL29763202M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL29763202M/Pax_Romana","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL29763202M/Pax_Romana","d